Experiment 3.1: Implement Queue using Stacks (Leetcode Problem 232)

Aim:Implement a First In First Out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support push, pop, peek, and empty operations.

Algorithm:

1.) Start
2.) Create two stacks s1 and s2.
3.) For the push(x) operation:
Move all elements from s1 to s2.
Push the new element x into s1.
Move all elements back from s2 to s1.
4.) For the pop() operation:
Remove the top element of s1 and return it.
5.) For the peek() operation:
Return the top element of s1 without removing it.
6.) For the empty() operation:
Check whether s1 is empty.
Return true if it is empty; otherwise, return false.
7.) End

Code:
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1;
    stack<int> s2;

    MyQueue() {

    }

    void push(int x) {
        while(!s1.empty()){
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }
        s1.push(x);
        while(!s2.empty()){
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }

    int pop() {
        int x=s1.top();
        s1.pop();
        return x;
    }

    int peek() {
        return s1.top();
    }

    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
    }
};

Experiment 3.2: Largest Rectangle in Histogram

Aim: Given an array of integers heights representing the histogram's bar heights where the width of each bar is 1, return the area of the largest rectangle in the histogram.

Algorithm:

1.)Initialize an empty stack and set the maximum area to 0.
2.)Add a 0 at the end of the heights array.
3.)Traverse the array from left to right.
4.)While the stack is not empty and the current height is smaller than the height at the stack top, pop the top index.
5.)Calculate the rectangle's height and width and update the maximum area.
6.)Push the current index into the stack.
7.)Return the maximum area.

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    int largestRectangleArea(vector<int>& heights) {
        stack<int> st;
        int ans = 0;
        heights.push_back(0);

        for (int i = 0; i < heights.size(); i++) {
            while (!st.empty() && heights[st.top()] > heights[i]) {
                int h = heights[st.top()];
                st.pop();

                int w = st.empty() ? i : i - st.top() - 1;
                ans = max(ans, h * w);
            }
            st.push(i);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
